  "summary": "Malicious code in crenelatts (PyPI)",
  "details": "\n---\n_-= Per source details. Do not edit below this line.=-_\n\n## Source: amazon-inspector (cc72e2a3431d0207f23fc8a8bdabadf7cc9fa262a15a25a31c2ca30a71a9eb38)\nPackage crenelatts version 0.1.0 on PyPI contains 13 files with no observed install-time network I/O, no suspicious lifecycle execution, no credential or environment scraping, no outbound exfiltration, no dropper, and no backdoor mechanism. No a static rule matches and no traced behavior indicate harm to an installer.\n\n## Source: kam193 (4ccd88fc743d2fd427510543af873fff8780bb4ec4916a565afb729315f28068)\nThis campaign consists of similar loader packages, which provide executing code from a given URL. While they do not contain the malicious payload and the usage remains unknown, they are clearly a coordinated campaign to place multiple deceptive ways to load malicious code.\n\n\n---\n\nCategory: MALICIOUS - The campaign has clearly malicious intent, like infostealers.\n\n\nCampaign: 2026-10-voice-synthesis-profiles\n\n\nReasons (based on the campaign):\n\n\n - Downloads and executes a remote malicious script.\n\n\n - other\n",
